  "question": {
    "text": "For changing the capacitance of a given paralle plate capacitor, a dielectric material of dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> is used, which has the same area as the plates of the capacitor. The thickness of the dielectric slab is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>d</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;is the separation between the plates of parallel plate capacitor. The new capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math> in terms of original capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is given by the following relation :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
